            <ArticleTitle>[The central regulation of pain sensitivity in rats after irradiation with high doses of ionizing radiation].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>183-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It was shown that during 24 h following whole-body exposure of male rats to gamma-quanta (150 Gy) the latent period of their response to the thermal effect increased a &quot;tail-flick&quot; test) and the threshold of the nociceptive response to an electric stimulus (the vocalization threshold) decreased. A correlation was found between the initial response to the nociceptive effects and variation of these values in irradiated animals.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
